IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nz-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `nz-part2-powers`

-- Tests for nz-part2-powers.l4 (ss 40 to 53).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section quoted beside it BEFORE the module was run.

§ `Section 40 -- Authority to make secondary legislation`

-- src:295 | It is not necessary for secondary legislation to refer to facts, circumstances, or preconditions that must exist or be satisfied before the legislation can be made.
#ASSERT `it is necessary for the secondary legislation to refer to the preconditions for making it` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `it is necessary for the secondary legislation to refer to the preconditions for making it` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:296 | Secondary legislation is not invalid just because the legislation under which it is expressed to have been made does not authorise its making as long as its making is authorised by other legislation.
-- The legislation it names authorises it: not invalid on this ground. It names legislation that does not authorise it, but other legislation does: still not invalid on this ground.
#ASSERT `secondary legislation is invalid because the legislation it is expressed to be made under does not authorise it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `secondary legislation is invalid because the legislation it is expressed to be made under does not authorise it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `secondary legislation is invalid because the legislation it is expressed to be made under does not authorise it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither authorises it: the section does not say.
#ASSERT `secondary legislation is invalid because the legislation it is expressed to be made under does not authorise it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 41 -- Secondary legislation may make consequential amendments to other secondary legislation`

-- src:298 | A power to make secondary legislation (the main secondary legislation) under one Act (the main Act) includes a power to make consequential amendments to other secondary legislation made by the same person (whether or not made under the same Act).
-- src:299 | An amendment is consequential for the purposes of this section if it is consequential on the passing or making of either or both of the following:
-- src:300 | the main Act or any amendment to it:
-- src:301 | the main secondary legislation or any amendment to it.
-- Made by the same person AND consequential on the main Act (or its amendment) or on the main secondary legislation (or its amendment).
#ASSERT `a power to make secondary legislation includes the power to make a consequential amendment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a power to make secondary legislation includes the power to make a consequential amendment` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a power to make secondary legislation includes the power to make a consequential amendment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a power to make secondary legislation includes the power to make a consequential amendment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a power to make secondary legislation includes the power to make a consequential amendment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a power to make secondary legislation includes the power to make a consequential amendment` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:302 | The only facts, circumstances, or preconditions that must exist or be satisfied before the consequential amendments are made are those (if any) for making the main secondary legislation.
#ASSERT `the preconditions for making consequential amendments` (LIST "the Minister has consulted") EQUALS LIST "the Minister has consulted"
#ASSERT `the preconditions for making consequential amendments` EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY

§ `Section 42 -- Amendments made to secondary legislation by Act do not prevent later amendments`

-- src:304 | Secondary legislation amended or replaced by an Act may be amended, revoked, or replaced by later secondary legislation as if the amendment or replacement had been made by secondary legislation.
#ASSERT `later secondary legislation may amend, revoke or replace secondary legislation amended or replaced by an Act` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `later secondary legislation may amend, revoke or replace secondary legislation amended or replaced by an Act` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 43 -- When powers can be exercised before commencement`

-- src:307 | A power conferred by legislation may be exercised before the legislation comes into force or takes effect to—
-- src:308 | make secondary legislation or another instrument; or
-- src:309 | serve a notice or document; or
-- src:310 | appoint a person to an office; or
-- src:311 | establish a body of persons; or
-- src:312 | confer or impose on a person a right, interest, title, immunity, duty, status, or capacity (a legal position); or
-- src:313 | do any other act or thing for the purposes of the legislation.
-- src:314 | However, the power may be exercised only if the exercise of the power is necessary or desirable—
-- src:315 | to bring the legislation into operation; or
-- src:316 | in connection with bringing the legislation into operation.
-- Each of the six kinds of act is allowed before commencement only if necessary or desirable to bring the legislation into operation, or in connection with that.
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `making secondary legislation or another instrument` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `making secondary legislation` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `making another instrument` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `serving a notice or document` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `serving a notice` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `serving a document` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `appointing a person to an office` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `establishing a body of persons` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `conferring or imposing a legal position on a person` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `conferring a legal position on a person` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `imposing a legal position on a person` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `doing another act or thing for the purposes of the legislation` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `making secondary legislation or another instrument` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `making secondary legislation` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `making another instrument` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `appointing a person to an office` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `doing another act or thing for the purposes of the legislation` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An act not for the purposes of the legislation is not one of the listed acts: the section does not say.
#ASSERT `a power may be exercised before the legislation comes into force to do` `doing an act or thing that is not for the purposes of the legislation` `when the exercise is necessary or desirable for bringing the legislation into operation:` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- src:317 | Subsection (1) applies as if—
-- src:318 | the legislation that confers the power, and all other legislation that is relevant to the power’s exercise and that has not yet commenced, had commenced; and
-- src:319 | a legal position that would be conferred or imposed by legislation that is relevant to the power’s exercise, and that has not yet commenced, has been conferred or imposed.
#ASSERT `the legislation is treated as having commenced for the purposes of section 43(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the legislation is treated as having commenced for the purposes of section 43(1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the legislation is treated as having commenced for the purposes of section 43(1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the legal position is treated as having been conferred or imposed for the purposes of section 43(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the legal position is treated as having been conferred or imposed for the purposes of section 43(1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the legal position is treated as having been conferred or imposed for the purposes of section 43(1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 44 -- Limit on when pre-commencement exercise of powers takes effect`

-- src:321 | Anything that results from the exercise of a power under section 43 may take effect only on and after the commencement of the legislation that confers the power.
-- src:322 | However, that limit does not apply if the exercise of the power is necessary or desirable—
-- src:323 | to bring the legislation into operation; or
-- src:324 | in connection with bringing the legislation into operation; or
-- src:325 | to amend, revoke, or replace anything previously done in reliance on section 43.
-- Takes effect on or after the commencement day: allowed. The day before: not, unless an exception applies.
#ASSERT `something resulting from a pre-commencement exercise may take effect on` (Date 1 7 2026) `when the legislation that confers the power commences on` (Date 1 7 2026) `if` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `something resulting from a pre-commencement exercise may take effect on` (Date 2 7 2026) `when the legislation that confers the power commences on` (Date 1 7 2026) `if` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `something resulting from a pre-commencement exercise may take effect on` (Date 30 6 2026) `when the legislation that confers the power commences on` (Date 1 7 2026) `if` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `something resulting from a pre-commencement exercise may take effect on` (Date 30 6 2026) `when the legislation that confers the power commences on` (Date 1 7 2026) `if` TRUE `or` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `something resulting from a pre-commencement exercise may take effect on` (Date 30 6 2026) `when the legislation that confers the power commences on` (Date 1 7 2026) `if` FALSE `or` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `something resulting from a pre-commencement exercise may take effect on` (Date 30 6 2026) `when the legislation that confers the power commences on` (Date 1 7 2026) `if` TRUE `or` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 45 -- Power to appoint person to an office includes related powers`

-- src:327 | The power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to—
-- src:328 | remove or suspend a person from the office:
-- src:329 | reappoint or reinstate a person to the office:
-- src:330 | appoint (temporarily or permanently, and for all or limited purposes) another person in place of a person who—
-- src:331 | has vacated the office voluntarily (for example, by resigning); or
-- src:332 | has died; or
-- src:333 | is absent temporarily or permanently; or
-- src:334 | is incapacitated temporarily or permanently in a way that affects the performance of that person's duty; or
-- src:335 | has been removed or suspended from the office.
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `remove or suspend a person from the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `reappoint or reinstate a person to the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who has vacated the office voluntarily` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who has died` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who is absent temporarily or permanently` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who is incapacitated in a way that affects the performance of that person's duty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who has been removed or suspended from the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Constituents of the printed items (ruling C); the incapacity that does not affect the duty is not in paragraph (c)(iv), and "includes" never excludes, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `remove a person from the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `suspend a person from the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `reappoint a person to the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `reinstate a person to the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who is absent temporarily` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who is absent permanently` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who is incapacitated temporarily in a way that affects the performance of that person's duty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who is incapacitated permanently in a way that affects the performance of that person's duty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who is incapacitated in a way that does not affect the performance of that person's duty` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who has been removed from the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `appoint another person in place of a person who has been suspended from the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power to` `another power` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 46 -- Power to do things may be exercised to correct errors`

-- src:337 | The power to do anything may be exercised to correct an error or omission in a previous exercise of the power.
