#ASSERT `the power may be exercised again` TRUE `even if the power is generally capable of being exercised more than once` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised again` FALSE `even if the power is generally capable of being exercised more than once` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised again` FALSE `even if the power is generally capable of being exercised more than once` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 47 -- Powers of office holder may be exercised by acting office holders`

-- src:340 | A power conferred on the holder of an office, other than a Minister of the Crown, may be exercised by 1 or both of the following:
-- src:341 | a person who is the holder’s deputy lawfully acting in the office:
-- src:342 | a person who is for the time being lawfully holding, or performing the duties of, the office.
#ASSERT `a power conferred on an office holder may be exercised by` `the holder's deputy lawfully acting in the office` `when the office holder is a Minister of the Crown:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power conferred on an office holder may be exercised by` `a person for the time being lawfully holding, or performing the duties of, the office` `when the office holder is a Minister of the Crown:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power conferred on an office holder may be exercised by` `a person for the time being lawfully holding the office` `when the office holder is a Minister of the Crown:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power conferred on an office holder may be exercised by` `a person for the time being lawfully performing the duties of the office` `when the office holder is a Minister of the Crown:` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power conferred on an office holder may be exercised by` `someone else` `when the office holder is a Minister of the Crown:` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a power conferred on an office holder may be exercised by` `someone else` `when the office holder is a Minister of the Crown:` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A Minister of the Crown is excluded: the section does not say.
#ASSERT `a power conferred on an office holder may be exercised by` `the holder's deputy lawfully acting in the office` `when the office holder is a Minister of the Crown:` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 48 -- Power to make includes power to amend or revoke`

-- src:344 | The power to make secondary legislation or any other instrument includes the power to—
-- src:345 | amend or revoke the legislation or instrument:
-- src:346 | replace the legislation or instrument.
-- src:347 | Requirements that apply in relation to making the secondary legislation or other instrument also apply, with all necessary modifications, in relation to its amendment, revocation, or replacement.
#ASSERT `the power to make secondary legislation or an instrument includes the power to` `amending it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make secondary legislation or an instrument includes the power to` `revoking it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make secondary legislation or an instrument includes the power to` `replacing it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to make secondary legislation or an instrument includes the power to` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the requirements for making it also apply, with necessary modifications, to` `amending it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirements for making it also apply, with necessary modifications, to` `revoking it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirements for making it also apply, with necessary modifications, to` `replacing it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirements for making it also apply, with necessary modifications, to` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 49 -- Power to make different provision for classes of matters`

-- src:349 | This section applies to legislation that confers on a person a power to make secondary legislation or any other instrument with respect to particular matters (however the matters are described).
-- src:350 | The power includes a power—
-- src:351 | to make the secondary legislation or instrument with respect to some only of those matters or with respect to a particular class or particular classes of those matters; and
-- src:352 | to make different provision with respect to different matters or different classes of matters.
#ASSERT `the power includes the power to use it by` `making it with respect to some only of the matters` `when the legislation confers a power with respect to particular matters:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes the power to use it by` `making it with respect to a particular class or classes of the matters` `when the legislation confers a power with respect to particular matters:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes the power to use it by` `making different provision with respect to different matters` `when the legislation confers a power with respect to particular matters:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes the power to use it by` `making different provision with respect to different classes of matters` `when the legislation confers a power with respect to particular matters:` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes the power to use it by` `another way` `when the legislation confers a power with respect to particular matters:` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The section applies only to a power with respect to particular matters.
#ASSERT `the power includes the power to use it by` `making it with respect to some only of the matters` `when the legislation confers a power with respect to particular matters:` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 50 -- Power to identify matters using classes`

-- src:354 | This section applies to legislation that confers on a person a power to make secondary legislation or any other instrument—
-- src:355 | declaring, prescribing, or specifying a matter; or
-- src:356 | doing anything in relation to a matter.
-- src:357 | In exercising the power, the person may identify the matter by referring to a class or classes of matters.
#ASSERT `the person may identify the matter by referring to a class or classes of matters` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person may identify the matter by referring to a class or classes of matters` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 51 -- Exercise or performance of powers, functions, and duties more than once`

-- src:359 | A power conferred by legislation may be exercised from time to time.
-- src:360 | A duty or function imposed by legislation may be performed from time to time.
#ASSERT `it may be exercised or performed from time to time` `a power conferred by legislation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `it may be exercised or performed from time to time` `a duty or function imposed by legislation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `it may be exercised or performed from time to time` `a duty imposed by legislation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `it may be exercised or performed from time to time` `a function imposed by legislation` EQUALS TRUE

§ `Section 52 -- Use of approved or prescribed forms`

-- src:363 | A form is not invalid just because it contains minor differences from an approved or a prescribed form as long as the form still has the same effect and is not misleading.
-- Minor differences, the same effect, and not misleading: not invalid just because of the differences.
#ASSERT `a form is invalid just because of its differences from the approved or prescribed form` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Each condition failing: the section does not say.
#ASSERT `a form is invalid just because of its differences from the approved or prescribed form` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a form is invalid just because of its differences from the approved or prescribed form` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a form is invalid just because of its differences from the approved or prescribed form` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

